      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Không sao đâu is the phrase to keep ready for \"It's okay\" in small service and first-contact moments. Say this when someone apologizes and you want to reassure them. It works best when you focus on using a short friendly phrase that invites a clear reply. After you say it, listen for a short reply, a smile, a time, or a light follow-up question; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
